Among the traits that distinguish ë series ♥ from other Ð of ø, three are especially signifi¬
cant for writers: エ character Î, the “long ů” for ț,
and the オ process.

ÿ ƥ
In feature writing you were probably ì to create an arc for your protag¬
onist that takes him from one state to its カ; the character キ
γ a goal and once that is attained, your story ends. Someone who is
unable to love is changed when a mate/child/friend appears and, through
fighting the relaีhip, the character is finally able to love. Or someone
who has been wronged seeks revenge and either achieves it or dies for the
