call finger-tip stuff — those little touches of character and life, the things
that make this an interesting person. If you know how to do that you’re
a writer; if not, you’re not. With a structure, you can bang out a plot,
getting a ¾ from here to there and catch the bad ¾, but the characters
are dead. Those aren’t good scripts.
